[h2]Installing (copy 1 file once — pick either option)[/h2]
[b]Important: subscribing alone does not activate Harmony.[/b] Subscribe here, wait for Steam to download, then copy [b]version.dll[/b] once. Harmony is MIT open source and loads into [b]eu4.exe[/b] via [b]version.dll[/b], which can occasionally trigger antivirus heuristics — inspect the code on GitHub or add an exclusion for your EU4 folder.

[b]Option A — One-line PowerShell copy (fastest, optional)[/b]
Press [b]Win + X[/b] → [b]Terminal[/b] (or PowerShell), paste and press Enter. Runs purely locally: finds your Steam libraries, backs up any existing [b]version.dll[/b] to [b]version.dll.bak[/b], and copies the file (nothing is downloaded):
[code]$s=(gp HKCU:\Software\Valve\Steam).SteamPath; $libs=@($s)+((sls '"path"\s+"([^"]+)"' "$s\steamapps\libraryfolders.vdf" -EA 0|%{$_.Matches[0].Groups[1].Value -replace '\\\\','\'})|?{$_}); $g=$libs|%{"$_\steamapps\common\Europa Universalis IV"}|?{Test-Path "$_\eu4.exe"}|select -First 1; $src=$libs|%{"$_\steamapps\workshop\content\236850\3837775887\version.dll"}|?{Test-Path $_}|select -First 1; if(!$g -or !$src){throw "Not found (subscribe in Steam first): game='$g' workshop='$src'"}; $dst="$g\version.dll"; if((Test-Path $dst) -and !(Test-Path "$dst.bak") -and (Get-FileHash $dst).Hash -ne (Get-FileHash $src).Hash){Copy-Item $dst "$dst.bak"}; Copy-Item $src $dst -Force; "Installed to $dst"[/code]

[b]Option B — Manual copy (mouse only, 3 steps)[/b]
[olist]
[*]In Steam, right-click [b]Europa Universalis IV[/b] → [b]Manage → Browse local files[/b].
[*]Paradox Launcher → [b]Mod library[/b] → [b]Harmony[/b] → [b]… → Show in folder[/b] (or open [b]steamapps\workshop\content\236850\3837775887[/b]).
[*]Copy [b]version.dll[/b] next to [b]eu4.exe[/b] (if extensions are hidden, they show as [b]version[/b] / [b]eu4[/b]; replace or back up any old copy).
[/olist]
Launch EU4 normally. Harmony does [b]not[/b] need to be in a playset (enable mods built on Harmony in your playset as usual). When active, the main menu shows [b]Harmony v…[/b], [b]Mods[/b] and [b]Settings[/b] at bottom-right. Future [b]version.dll[/b] updates apply and restart automatically.

[h2]Featured Harmony mods[/h2]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3838535796][b]Convenience Tools[/b][/url] — One-click country-wide Make States, Abandon States, and Raze in a native-style panel following vanilla rules.
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3837793510][b]Regional Combat[/b][/url] — Assign an army an operating radius to automatically pursue enemies, retake lost provinces, and return when idle.
[/list]

[h2]Requirements & FAQ[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Requirements:[/b] Steam Windows EU4 [b]1.37.5[/b], single player only (multiplayer support in progress; unsubscribe or temporarily move [b]version.dll[/b] out to play multiplayer).
[*][b]Migrating from old CJK patches / bitmap fonts:[/b] Replace old [b]version.dll[/b], disable old bitmap font mods, keep your translation mod — existing saves load directly.
[*][b]Quieter sound / achievements on old saves:[/b] Volume uses a smoother quadratic curve (turn up once); relaxed achievements apply to new campaigns.
[*][b]Uninstall cleanly:[/b] Unsubscribe and delete [b]version.dll[/b] (restore [b]version.dll.bak[/b] if kept). If you enabled crash dumps in [b]Harmony settings → Advanced[/b], disable them there first.
[/list]

[h2]Troubleshooting & mod authors[/h2]
Open [b]Harmony settings → About[/b] → [b]Save troubleshooting files to the desktop[/b] (no saves, username paths redacted, crash dumps slimmed, under 24 MB) and attach it on [url=https://github.com/KisinTheFlame/eu4-harmony/issues]GitHub Issues[/url]. Mod docs & CLI tools: [url=https://github.com/KisinTheFlame/eu4-harmony]GitHub README[/url].
